{"bill":{"id":"119-hjres-14","congress":119,"billType":"hjres","billNumber":"14","title":"Proposing an amendment to the Constitution of the United States to repeal the sixteenth article of amendment.","introducedDate":"2025-01-09","latestActionDate":"2025-04-07","latestActionText":"Message on Senate action sent to the House.","policyArea":"Taxation","subjects":["Constitution and constitutional amendments","Tax administration and collection, taxpayers","Tax reform and tax simplification"],"sponsorBioguideId":"D000626","cosponsorBioguideIds":["M001212","M001184"],"committeeCodes":[],"committeeNames":[],"officialSummary":"This joint resolution proposes a constitutional amendment repealing the Sixteenth Amendment to the Constitution. The Sixteenth Amendment to the Constitution, ratified in 1913, specifies that Congress may collect federal income taxes.","congressDotGovUrl":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-joint-resolution/14","source":"congress","sourceUrl":"https://www.govinfo.gov/bulkdata/BILLSTATUS/119/hjres/BILLSTATUS-119hjres14.xml","fetchedAt":"2026-07-29T01:30:17.993Z"},"classification":{"billId":"119-hjres-14","plainSummary":"This joint resolution proposes a constitutional amendment that would eliminate the Sixteenth Amendment, which currently allows Congress to collect federal income taxes. Ratified in 1913, the Sixteenth Amendment established the legal foundation for the federal income tax system. If this amendment were adopted, Congress would lose its constitutional authority to levy income taxes unless a different revenue mechanism were authorized.","industries":[{"industry":"finance-banking","confidence":0.7,"rationale":"Elimination of federal income tax would fundamentally alter tax-advantaged investment products, retirement accounts, and financial planning services that banks offer."},{"industry":"insurance","confidence":0.6,"rationale":"Many insurance products are structured around current income tax treatment, including life insurance, annuities, and health savings accounts."},{"industry":"real-estate","confidence":0.6,"rationale":"Real estate investment relies heavily on income tax deductions for mortgage interest, depreciation, and capital gains treatment."},{"industry":"legal","confidence":0.5,"rationale":"Tax law and compliance constitute a significant portion of legal practice; eliminating income tax would reshape demand for these services."}],"method":"llm","model":"claude-sonnet-4-5","inputHash":"8716fa3542d5d648838c8807","classifiedAt":"2026-07-30T02:49:07.867Z"},"plain":{"whatItDoes":"This joint resolution would propose a constitutional amendment repealing the Sixteenth Amendment to the Constitution.","whoItTouches":"Anyone who pays federal tax.","everydayEffect":"If it passed, the change would show up in your tax bill. Nothing has changed yet. Most bills never become law.","confidence":"crs-summary","source":"Reworded from the official summary. Staff at the Congressional Research Service wrote that summary. It is public domain, and the full text of it is further down this page.","titleInPlainWords":null},"overlaps":[{"billId":"119-hjres-14","bioguideId":"D000626","cycle":2026,"score":0.06771612353130639,"matches":[{"industry":"finance-banking","donorAmount":83000,"donorShare":0.13732809170207416,"billConfidence":0.7,"contribution":0.0400540267464383},{"industry":"insurance","donorAmount":29500,"donorShare":0.04880938199049623,"billConfidence":0.6,"contribution":0.012202345497624058},{"industry":"real-estate","donorAmount":20500,"donorShare":0.033918384095090605,"billConfidence":0.6,"contribution":0.008479596023772651},{"industry":"legal","donorAmount":20250,"donorShare":0.03350474526466267,"billConfidence":0.5,"contribution":0.00698015526347139}],"method":{"formula":"score = Σ_industries ( donorShare(industry) × billWeight(industry) ), where billWeight = classifierConfidence / Σ classifierConfidence. Range 0–1, read as a weighted share of disclosed itemized money.","donorProfileCycle":